<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The shockwave ring a Breach Jump or Breach Burn leaves where it lands, on a planet and in
    space alike, fired by SCWC_BreachLanding as the SCWC_Breach explosion's centre effecter.
    The jump's one distortion effect: a matching ring at the space launch cell was tried and
    dropped on 2026-09-18 so nothing competes with the landing for the player's eye.

    Recipe: Core's impact wave (ShockwaveFast, the Anomaly pit gate's emergence ring; Biotech's
    mech-band stun shockwave is the same at pawn scale): a black quad on the
    MoteLargeDistortionWave shader, which sweeps a ring of background distortion outward over
    the fleck's age (Graphic_FleckPulse feeds it AgeSecs). Chosen 2026-09-18 over the first
    version, a FleckGlowDistortBackground disc on the PsycastDistortionMask ripple texture
    (Core's psycast area ring, scaled fast): that read as a psycast, this reads as an impact.
    Everything referenced here is Core-owned, so no DLC is needed: the shaderType, the
    textures and FleckBase; Core's own ShockwaveFast and Fleck_HeatWaveDistortion use them.

    Two departures from the vanilla wave rings, both because in play the ring showed a
    rotational, spiral-like component that the greyscale masks cannot produce (decoded: R, G
    and B identical on every lit pixel, so no displacement vectors) and the sprayer does not
    add (rotationRate defaults to 0). _noiseIntensity 0 (shader default 2, with
    _ageToNoiseRatio 100 scrolling the 128x1 PsycastNoise strip by age): the one animated
    non-radial input; zeroing it softened the twist. _DistortionTex is
    MoteHellfireCannon_HeatWaveDistortion (one ragged spoke-free band) instead of the
    PsychicDistortionCurrents torus, whose radial spokes gave the sweep something to appear to
    turn; that removed it. Vanilla's rings keep both defaults and the twist.

    Sizing: a fleck's width is drawSize x (1 + growthRate x age), and the shader's ring runs
    within that quad (its sweep timing is compiled in and was tuned by eye). growthRate 1.5 is
    the value every vanilla instance of this recipe uses, so drawSize sets the size: 4.5 over
    0.40 s ends at 7.2 cells across, clearing the breach footprint (breachRadius 2 on the
    ability extension, a 5-cell-wide disc) so it reads as the impact spreading past the
    rubble, not lost under it. Timings follow the mech-band shockwave's shape (fade in 0.04,
    hold, fade out 0.10) at less than half its life. _distortionIntensity 0.066 is the
    mech-band value, the one physical stun shockwave in the game; the range shipped for THIS
    shader runs 0.05 to 0.2 (ShockwaveFast, a screen-filling map event), and the number means
    something else under other shaders. MoteOverheadLow, as the mech-band ring: draws over the
    wearer and whoever else stands in the blast, while the Bomb-style cell flecks on
    MoteOverhead, one layer up, still burst over it. drawOffscreen true so the sprayer still
    spawns it with the camera elsewhere; a one-shot fleck, so it costs nothing. If
    breachRadius changes, rescale drawSize with it.
  -->
  <FleckDef ParentName="FleckBase">
    <defName>SCWC_BreachLandingShockwave</defName>
    <altitudeLayer>MoteOverheadLow</altitudeLayer>
    <fadeInTime>0.04</fadeInTime>
    <solidTime>0.26</solidTime>
    <fadeOutTime>0.10</fadeOutTime>
    <growthRate>1.5</growthRate>
    <drawOffscreen>true</drawOffscreen>
    <graphicData>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_FleckPulse</graphicClass>
      <texPath>Things/Mote/Black</texPath>
      <shaderType>MoteLargeDistortionWave</shaderType>
      <shaderParameters>
        <_DistortionTex>/Things/Mote/MoteHellfireCannon_HeatWaveDistortion</_DistortionTex>
        <_NoiseTex>/Things/Mote/PsycastNoise</_NoiseTex>
        <_distortionIntensity>0.066</_distortionIntensity>
        <_brightnessMultiplier>1.15</_brightnessMultiplier>
        <_noiseIntensity>0</_noiseIntensity>
      </shaderParameters>
      <drawSize>4.5</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
  </FleckDef>
</Defs>
